A||N||4||DaveL||Speedometer not up to speed||||5||
Z||000000||DaveL||01-26-2000||04:17 PM||||My speedometer goes off at odd times. A light tap on the top of the instrument cluster makes it go again. The same for the tachometer. It would seem to be a loose connection, but I'm a little afraid to remove the cluster covers. Could it be a simple fix ??||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||01-26-2000||06:20 PM||||take off the covers, pull the 3 connectors off and reseat them. that would be the first thing. not hard. 2 are in back, one is under.||||reg||1
Z||000002||daved||01-26-2000||09:21 PM||||I dont see any common electrical connections, +12 volt or grounds between the Tach. & Speedo. I assume this is sporadic and neither go off together.  For instance, a power supply problem to the Tach. would also effect the fuel gauge at the same time!  Think O. is correct.  Pretty cheap printed circuit sockets that the plugs go into.  If you see any corrosion on the plug connection surfaces, polish them with a pencil eraser...but be sure to wipe off all the little crumbs left behind with a clean cloth...a cotton T-shirt or similar.  The PC sockets are copper, and almost impossible to get at to clean in place, but rarely are a problem ( unless someone spilled Coke in there!)   ||||reg||1
Z||000003||David Gamache||01-26-2000||10:09 PM||||It is not uncommon for the brass connectors to get a little tarnished with a green build up and cause a bad connection. Check the plugs on the back of the speedo as everyone else recommended. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||DaveL||01-27-2000||08:23 AM||||Sounds hopefull. I'll try this weekend. Yeah, they go on and off independently of each other. Sometimes when I tap the top of the cluster to get the speedo going, the tach goes off and the speedo goes on. I think it may be haunted. I also have some electrical contact spray cleaner which I'll try.||||reg||1
